Details
Performance Metrics and Outlier Removal: Rowie and Christine Pinza discussed overall smiling core scores moving slightly from 74.80 to 75.24, noting that significant improvements were visible on a per-site level. Christine Pinza attributed a 7% simulated improvement specifically to the removal of outliers in core. Christson intervened to redirect the discussion toward tangible factors to avoid dragging out the meeting (00:01:16).

Data Validation Recommendations and Volume Analysis: Christson recommended validating data starting with volume to determine if Shopify's process restrictions and pain points have decreased during BFCM (00:02:29). Christson also suggested examining DAT, CESAT, and neutral scores to see if customer satisfaction improved (00:03:27). Regarding outliers, Carl and Nitin Rana confirmed that the removed individuals were taken off chats about a month or two before being entirely removed from the system, meaning they could not account for recent metric changes (00:04:32).

New Hire Schedule Shifts and Performance Trends: Carl highlighted that shifting new hire schedules in PH to non-peak hours during the first week of November helped arrest performance hits from October (00:05:41). Rowie noted having second thoughts about this attribution because upward performance trends began even before the official schedule movement, though Rowie agreed to look into it further (00:06:40).

OMG Launch and Be Human Initiative: Rowie and Carl clarified that the be human initiative in August differed from the OMG launch, which focused on bringing back transformational behaviors where staff acknowledge stores and engage in focused discussions (00:08:05). Carl expressed frustration that despite positive numbers, the team lacked a clear handle on what specifically drove the impact, emphasizing the need to track operational outputs like team leader performance and ticket quality (00:09:04).

Preparation for EMBR and Score Discrepancies: Carl expressed frustration with the lack of preparation for the EMBR deck, noting that weekly operations brief data should have been readily integrated instead of starting from scratch (00:10:05). Christine Pinza apologized and explained the confusion arose from distinguishing between an insights MBR and a standard MBR, and Christine Pinza also clarified that a recent score of 78 referred strictly to chat interactions rather than the overall smiley score of 75 (00:11:06).

Crafting the Narrative for October and November: Carl and Christson discussed how October represents a flat recovery story while November shows a distinct upward lift (00:14:21) (00:17:18). Christson warned that attributing the entire recovery solely to internal operational actions presents an incomplete story to Shopify, because it implies previous process bottlenecks were never genuine constraints and risks failing to explain future drops in consistency (00:18:08).

Concurrency and Contact Complexity Analysis: Carl noted that concurrency increased from 1.3 or 1.4 in September and October to 1.6 in November, introducing higher operational complexity alongside improved smiley performance (00:19:50). Paulene reported that contact complexity remained flat through September and October while requiring validation for November, and Paulene added that retail case study updates were available. Carl and Christson agreed to remove the C++ and C- grading system from the presentation deck (00:21:13).

Executive Summary and Forward-Looking EMBR Structure: Carl and Christine Pinza agreed to remove vendor ranking and grading systems from slide eight to avoid governance issues, opting instead for an executive summary focusing on key wins, top focus areas, and a running update from October to November (00:24:34). Carl outlined that the presentation should cover the merchant journey under double concurrency and preview December readiness across core, retail, plus, and tier-2 core combined premium segments as a forward-looking conversation rather than a past performance review (00:26:36).

Presentation Assignments and Next Steps: Carl assigned presentation responsibilities for the upcoming meeting, asking Rowie to discuss the global OMG rollout, Paulene to cover QA contributions, directors Nitin Rana and Summit to prepare site-level confidence updates for December, and Christine Pinza to own the performance summary (00:29:06). Carl concluded with instructions to finalize the deck in an extended meeting following the next day's standup (00:31:19).

